      "title": "International Internships",
      "description": "International Internships | Global Learning at Nichols College Skip to Content Info For Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni Visit Apply Give Menu Visit Apply Give Close Academics Academics at Nichols Find Your Program Undergraduate Programs Academics Undergraduate Programs Undergraduate Academics Bachelor of Science in Business Administration Bachelor of Arts Accelerated Programs Certificates Online Programs Minors Honors Program Graduate Programs Academics Graduate Programs Graduate Academics College Catalog Academic Services Academic Calendar Admissions Welcome to Nichols Visit Us Undergraduate Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions First Year Students International Students Military Students Online Students Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Meet The Admissions Team Graduate Admissions Net Price Calculator Student Life Explore Student Life at Nichols Student Involvement Student Belonging Residence Life Student Life Residence Life ResLife at Nichols Housing Dining Fitness and Recreation Student Activities Student Life Student Activities Clubs and Organizations Tradition and Events Our Campus Student Support and Safety Student Life Student Support and Safety Support and Safety at Nichols Health and Wellness Campus Safety Student Support Services Commuters Support Services Career Readiness Career Readiness Professional Development Career Readiness Professional Development Professional Development at Nichols Signature Leadership Programs Professional Development Seminar Emerging Leaders Program Lead 120 Student-Run Opportunities Experiential Learning Career Readiness Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Overview Internships Global Learning Study Abroad (Study Away) International Internships Faculty Led Travel Career and Professional Development Center About About Us Nichols at a Glance History and Accreditation Leadership Offices Directory Directions Contact Quick Links Athletics Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni Career Readiness Experiential Learning Global Learning International Internships at Nichols College In This Section Career Readiness Professional Development Professional Development at Nichols Signature Leadership Programs Professional Development Seminar Emerging Leaders Program Lead 120 Student-Run Opportunities Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Overview Internships Global Learning Study Abroad (Study Away) International Internships Faculty Led Travel Career and Professional Development Center International internships give Nichols College students the chance to gain professional experience while immersing themselves in another culture. Supported by the Office for International Engagement , these opportunities help students build real-world skills, strengthen their resumes and stand out in a competitive global job market. International internships allow students to fulfill the experiential learning requirements of their program. Where Can You Intern Abroad? Students can pursue internships in global business centers, nonprofit organizations, cultural institutions and industry-specific placements around the world. Programs are designed to align with academic goals while offering meaningful hands-on experience. Planning Your Trip Office for International Engagement helps students explore internship options, navigate applications, understand academic requirements and prepare for living abroad. Support includes advising, documentation guidance and coordination to ensure credits apply toward degree programs. Learn More About Studying Abroad at Nichols College Ready to Go Beyond the Classroom? From a simple approval process through our Office for International Engagement to special advising all along the way, we’re here to help you plan your international internship. To find out more, contact us at study.abroad@nichols.edu . Email Us FAQ Frequently Asked Questions Do international internships count toward my major or minor? Often, international internships can count towards your major or minor and help fulfill your experiential learning requirement. Do I need prior work experience? Most international internship programs don’t require extensive work experience. The Office for International Engagement will help you find a match for your academic interests and experience. Are international internships paid? This depends on the program. Some internships may offer stipends, while others may be unpaid, depending on the field and the country. Students are encouraged to apply for external scholarships or funding in advance of their program. What types of industries offer international internships? Students may find opportunities in business, marketing, finance, communications, hospitality, education, nonprofit work, cultural organizations and other fields that align with their academic interests. Is there financial support for international internships? Yes, the College launched SELF (Student Experiential Learning Fund) in 2021 to help subsidize expenses related to external internships, experiential learning opportunities and study abroad (study away). Learn more here . INFO FOR Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni HELPFUL LINKS Maps and Directions Work at Nichols Contact Us Athletics News STUDENT RESOURCES Course Catalog Academic Calendar Nichols Hub OneLogin Events Request a Transcript 800-470-3379 121 Center Rd PO Box 5000 Dudley, MA, 01571 Title IX Privacy ©Nichols College 2026 Close Quick Links Athletics Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni"
    },
    "https://www.nichols.edu/career-readiness/experiential-learning/global-learning/faculty-led-travel/": {
      "title": "Faculty-Led Travel Abroad",
      "description": "Faculty-Led Travel Programs | Nichols College Skip to Content Info For Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni Visit Apply Give Menu Visit Apply Give Close Academics Academics at Nichols Find Your Program Undergraduate Programs Academics Undergraduate Programs Undergraduate Academics Bachelor of Science in Business Administration Bachelor of Arts Accelerated Programs Certificates Online Programs Minors Honors Program Graduate Programs Academics Graduate Programs Graduate Academics College Catalog Academic Services Academic Calendar Admissions Welcome to Nichols Visit Us Undergraduate Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions First Year Students International Students Military Students Online Students Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Meet The Admissions Team Graduate Admissions Net Price Calculator Student Life Explore Student Life at Nichols Student Involvement Student Belonging Residence Life Student Life Residence Life ResLife at Nichols Housing Dining Fitness and Recreation Student Activities Student Life Student Activities Clubs and Organizations Tradition and Events Our Campus Student Support and Safety Student Life Student Support and Safety Support and Safety at Nichols Health and Wellness Campus Safety Student Support Services Commuters Support Services Career Readiness Career Readiness Professional Development Career Readiness Professional Development Professional Development at Nichols Signature Leadership Programs Professional Development Seminar Emerging Leaders Program Lead 120 Student-Run Opportunities Experiential Learning Career Readiness Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Overview Internships Global Learning Study Abroad (Study Away) International Internships Faculty Led Travel Career and Professional Development Center About About Us Nichols at a Glance History and Accreditation Leadership Offices Directory Directions Contact Quick Links Athletics Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni Career Readiness Experiential Learning Global Learning Faculty-Led Travel Abroad at Nichols College In This Section Career Readiness Professional Development Professional Development at Nichols Signature Leadership Programs Professional Development Seminar Emerging Leaders Program Lead 120 Student-Run Opportunities Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Overview Internships Global Learning Study Abroad (Study Away) International Internships Faculty Led Travel Career and Professional Development Center Traveling Abroad with Faculty at Nichols Faculty-led travel programs allow Nichols College students to explore the world alongside expert professors who integrate global learning directly into their coursework. These 1-2 week structured trips combine academic study with real-world exposure and are coordinated through the Center for International Studies. Where Can You Go With Faculty-Led Programs? Depending on the course and faculty leader, students may visit international cities, business hubs, historical regions or cultural landmarks. Each trip is intentionally designed to align with classroom concepts, making global learning an extension of the academic experience. The College currently offers a two-week trip to Costa Rica between semesters. Planning Your Trip Nichols faculty, the Center for International Studies and our travel partner provider design the trip, which is embedded within a course. Nichols faculty and staff support students with travel preparation, financial planning and academic expectations. Students travel confidently knowing they are learning in a structured, intentional environment. Learn More About Study Abroad at Nichols College Living through someone else’s culture has deepened my eagerness to learn more about other cultures, and it’s made me want to share my passion of traveling with others and teach them how important it is to travel the world and gain new experiences. —Gabrielle Maranchie ’27 on her and her fellow classmates’ takeaways on their two-week faculty-led excursion to Costa Rica. Ready to Go Beyond the Classroom? From a simple approval process through our Office for International Engagement to special advising all along the way, we’re here to help. To find out more, contact us at study.abroad@nichols.edu . Email Us FAQ Frequently Asked Questions Do I need to know another language? No. Faculty-led trips are taught and guided in English. What is included in the cost of a faculty-led trip? Typically transportation, housing, select meals, program fees and academic activities comprise the cost of a faculty-led trip. Exact details vary depending on the trip. Can I join a faculty-led trip outside my major? Often yes, depending on the course requirements and available spots on the trip. Students must be enrolled in the course tied to the trip. Will faculty-led travel impact my graduation plan? No! These trips are tied directly to an existing course and are part of the Nichols College curriculum. How big are the travel groups? The travel groups are small, usually not more than 10-15 students. Are accommodations arranged for me? Yes, housing logistics for faculty-led travel are handled by Nichols College or the partnering travel provider. INFO FOR Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni HELPFUL LINKS Maps and Directions Work at Nichols Contact Us Athletics News STUDENT RESOURCES Course Catalog Academic Calendar Nichols Hub OneLogin Events Request a Transcript 800-470-3379 121 Center Rd PO Box 5000 Dudley, MA, 01571 Title IX Privacy ©Nichols College 2026 Close Quick Links Athletics Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni"
    },
    "https://www.nichols.edu/career-readiness/career-and-professional-development-center/": {
      "title": "Career and Professional Development Center",
      "description": "Career & Professional Development Center | Nichols College Skip to Content Info For Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni Visit Apply Give Menu Visit Apply Give Close Academics Academics at Nichols Find Your Program Undergraduate Programs Academics Undergraduate Programs Undergraduate Academics Bachelor of Science in Business Administration Bachelor of Arts Accelerated Programs Certificates Online Programs Minors Honors Program Graduate Programs Academics Graduate Programs Graduate Academics College Catalog Academic Services Academic Calendar Admissions Welcome to Nichols Visit Us Undergraduate Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions First Year Students International Students Military Students Online Students Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Meet The Admissions Team Graduate Admissions Net Price Calculator Student Life Explore Student Life at Nichols Student Involvement Student Belonging Residence Life Student Life Residence Life ResLife at Nichols Housing Dining Fitness and Recreation Student Activities Student Life Student Activities Clubs and Organizations Tradition and Events Our Campus Student Support and Safety Student Life Student Support and Safety Support and Safety at Nichols Health and Wellness Campus Safety Student Support Services Commuters Support Services Career Readiness Career Readiness Professional Development Career Readiness Professional Development Professional Development at Nichols Signature Leadership Programs Professional Development Seminar Emerging Leaders Program Lead 120 Student-Run Opportunities Experiential Learning Career Readiness Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Overview Internships Global Learning Study Abroad (Study Away) International Internships Faculty Led Travel Career and Professional Development Center About About Us Nichols at a Glance History and Accreditation Leadership Offices Directory Directions Contact Quick Links Athletics Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni Career Readiness Career and Professional Development Center at Nichols College Your career success starts here. In This Section Career Readiness Professional Development Professional Development at Nichols Signature Leadership Programs Professional Development Seminar Emerging Leaders Program Lead 120 Student-Run Opportunities Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Overview Internships Global Learning Study Abroad (Study Away) International Internships Faculty Led Travel Career and Professional Development Center At Nichols College Career and Professional Development Center (CPDC), you'll gain the skills, connections and confidence to launch a successful career you love. Located in the Fels Student Center, the CPDC offers personalized career coaching, interview preparation, professional tools such as Handshake, Big Interview, and SkillsFirst and access to exclusive employer connections throughout New England and beyond. Whether you’re exploring career options as a first-year student , searching for your first internship or preparing for post-graduation employment, you’ll find the resources and guidance you need. From on-campus recruiting events to our professional clothing boutique , we’ve designed our services around one goal: helping you transition from classroom to career with self-assurance. Plus, our commitment doesn’t end at graduation—you’ll have lifetime access to all CPDC services as a Nichols alumnus. Comprehensive Career Services Designed for Your Success See how the Career and Professional Development Center can help you succeed. Career Planning and Exploration You don't need to have all the answers on day one. Our career coaches help you explore different paths, identify your strengths and develop a strategic plan that aligns with your goals. Through one-on-one coaching sessions, career assessments and industry research tools, you'll gain clarity about your future. We offer scheduled appointments to fit your needs, making it easy to get the guidance you need when you need it most. Schedule an Appointment with a Career Coach Resume and Interview Preparation First impressions matter. Our team helps you craft compelling resumes and cover letters that showcase your unique experience and skills. You'll also develop interview strategies through mock interviews and feedback sessions in our interview suites. We have two meeting rooms that students can reserve for their web based or phone interviews. Need professional attire in a pinch? Visit our Bison Boutique to borrow interview clothing for presentations, career fairs and job interviews. Learn More About the Bison Boutique Internship and Job Search Support Finding the right opportunity is easier with the right support system. Our online jobs and internships board connects you with employers who are particularly familiar with and value Nichols students for internships and full-time positions. We'll help you navigate job search strategies, understand different industries and identify opportunities that match your career interests. Whether you're looking for a summer internship or a full-time position after graduation, we'll guide you through the application process from start to finish. Visit our Online Jobs and Internships Board Connect With Employers Who Want to Hire You Career and Internship Fairs Every year, more than 70 employers visit campus specifically to meet Nichols students. Our Career and Internship Fair each February brings together diverse companies and organizations—from Kraft Sports Group to the United States Secret Service to Mohegan Sun and The Cigna Group. You’ll also have access to specialized recruiting events like our Business by the Numbers Fair in September, designed to connect you with employers in your specific field of study. Master the Art of Professional Networking Year-Round Networking Programs Networking is a Nichols-embraced and critical career skill that opens doors throughout your professional life. That’s why we offer structured networking opportunities throughout the year, starting from your sophomore year. At our Annual Second Year Success event you’ll connect with successful Nichols alumni who can offer guidance and potential internship opportunities. Our Career Exploration Nights feature alumni panels who share insider perspectives on the hiring process in their industries. Explore Networking Opportunities Lifetime Career Support, Even After Graduation As a Nichols College alumnus, you’ll have permanent access to all our career services, whether you graduated last year or twenty years ago. Need help with a career transition? We’re here to support you at every stage of your professional journey. This lifetime commitment reflects our investment in your long-term success. Visit the Career and Professional Development Center Location: Fels Student Center Hours: Monday-Friday, 8:30 AM – 4:30 PM Phone: (508) 213-2489 Email: cpdc@nichols.edu For Employers: Interested in hiring talented Nichols students for internships or full-time positions? Learn More About Recruiting at Nichols College. Visit the Career and Professional Development Center CPDC Office FAQ FAQs About Our Career and Professional Development Center When should I start using CPDC services? We encourage first year students to explore career options, begin building their resumes and attend networking events. The earlier you engage with the CPDC, the more prepared you’ll be for internships and post-graduation employment. Do I need an appointment to visit the CPDC? We offer both scheduled appointments. Walk-in hours are available Monday through Friday from 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM, but we recommend scheduling an appointment for longer career planning sessions or resume reviews. What is the Bison Boutique? The Bison Boutique is our professional clothing and accessories resource where you can borrow brand-new interview attire for career fairs, interviews and professional presentations. This free service ensures all students have access to professional clothing when they need it most. Can alumni use CPDC services? Yes, all Nichols College alumni have lifetime access to CPDC services, including career advising, resume reviews, job search assistance and our wide array of licensed resources. Whether you graduated last year or decades ago, we’re here to support your career growth. How many employers attend Nichols career fairs? Our Career and Internship Fair attracts more than 60 employers to campus each year, representing diverse industries from finance and technology to sports management and public service. We also host specialized fairs focused on specific fields. What kinds of companies recruit at Nichols? We work with a wide range of employers, from Fortune 500 companies like CVS Health, Travelers and Cigna, to celebrated regional firms such as AAFCPAs, E-Clinical Works, Mohegan Sun and Kraft Sports Group, to important nonprofits like OU Inc., Boys and Girls Club and L.U.K Crisis Center. Our Central Massachusetts location provides strong connections to employers throughout Worcester County, Massachusetts and capital cities in New England, including Boston, Providence and Hartford. INFO FOR Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni HELPFUL LINKS Maps and Directions Work at Nichols Contact Us Athletics News STUDENT RESOURCES Course Catalog Academic Calendar Nichols Hub OneLogin Events Request a Transcript 800-470-3379 121 Center Rd PO Box 5000 Dudley, MA, 01571 Title IX Privacy ©Nichols College 2026 Close Quick Links Athletics Prospective Students Current Students and Families Current Faculty and Staff Alumni"
    }
